nd errors (queue 242; Python/initconfig.c's config_get_stdio_errors and"] [203 1 "// pylifecycle.c's create_stdio): PYTHONIOENCODING=ENCODING[:ERRORS] (ignored under -E and -I) forces the encoding and"] [204 1 "// the errors of stdin and stdout; stderr's errors stay backslashreplace. Without ERRORS they are strict, and"] [205 1 "// surrogateescape when no encoding is forced and the locale (LC_ALL, else LC_CTYPE, else LANG) is C or POSIX, as the"] [206 1 "// coerced C locale's. An unset locale keeps strict (pyi has no coercion to model)."] [267 1 "// writeStr is TextIOWrapper.write's encoding: utf-8 with strict errors as before, else the codec of PYTHONIOENCODING"] [268 1 "// and the stream's errors handler (a UnicodeEncodeError for an error left strict)."] [272 19 "// reconfigure()'s (queue 286)"] [290 1 "// The site module's exit and quit (site.py's Quitter; _sitebuiltins): calling one raises SystemExit(code)."] [315 1 "// site's help (_sitebuiltins._Helper, queue 587): calling it imports pydoc and calls pydoc.help (test_pydoc's"] [316 1 "// test_fail_help_cli: python -c \"help()\")."] [347 1 "// startOrigArgv is sys.orig_argv: bin/pyi python passes the executable and its command line in PYI_ORIG_ARGV (joined"] [348 1 "// by the unit separator), read once and removed from the environment."] [362 1 "// fsDecodeString is a command line's or the environment's bytes as a str: UTF-8 with surrogateescape (Py_DecodeLocale;"] [363 1 "// py-os-1124)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[46 12] [46 25] [86 59] [109 63] [119 57] [140 60] [149 54] [157 64] [162 65] [177 34] [181 67] [185 7] [185 30] [191 39] [223 41] [368 60]]} (go/file "builtins_sys_info.go" :imports [


